/-!
# The stable hat invariant of a multipointed Heegaard diagram

Ozsváth, Stipsicz and Szabó define a combinatorial three-manifold invariant from the hat complex of
a nice multipointed Heegaard diagram. Its homology `\widetilde{HF}(D)` depends on the number
`b(D)` of basepoints: adding a basepoint tensors it with the two-dimensional space `W = 𝔽 ⊕ 𝔽`. So
the invariant is the class `HF̂_st(D) = [\widetilde{HF}(D), b(D)]` of the pair under the
equivalence relation on pairs `(V, b)` of a finite-dimensional vector space and a natural number
generated by `(V ⊗ W^{⊗ k}, b + k) ~ (V, b)`.

**Stable classes.** Tensoring with `W` doubles the dimension, so `dim V / 2 ^ b` is constant on a
class. It also determines the class: if `dim V / 2 ^ b = dim V' / 2 ^ (b + k)` then
`V' ≅ V ⊗ W^{⊗ k}`, since finite-dimensional spaces of equal dimension are isomorphic
(`TauCeti.stableClass_eq_stableClass_add_iff`). So two pairs are equivalent exactly when they are
related by a single generating move, and the class of `(V, b)` is recorded by the rational number
`TauCeti.stableClass K V b = dim V / 2 ^ b`. The class records the number of basepoints: `[𝔽, 1]`
and `[𝔽², 1]` differ, although `𝔽² ≅ 𝔽 ⊗ W`, so that a relation adding factors of `W` without
counting them would identify them.

**The invariant of a diagram.** For a Heegaard diagram whose hat differential `∂` squares to zero,
`TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.hatHomology` is the homology `\widetilde{HF}(D) = ker ∂ ⧸ im ∂` and
`TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.hatStableClass` its class with the number of basepoints. These
definitions assume no niceness. For a nice diagram (`TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.IsNice`) the
class is the Ozsváth–Stipsicz–Szabó invariant `HF̂_st(D)`; for other diagrams it is only the
stable class of the homology of the count of index-one domains. That `∂ ∘ ∂ = 0` for every nice
diagram (Ozsváth–Stipsicz–Szabó, Theorem 6.11) is not proved here, so these definitions take it
as an argument. It holds for the genus-one diagrams of lens
spaces and of `S¹ × S²` below, whose differentials vanish, and it passes along the two
stabilizations:

* **Type `g`.** Stabilizing in a region (`TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.stabilize`) does not change
  the hat complex, so it does not change `\widetilde{HF}(D)`
  (`TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.hatHomologyStabilizeEquiv`) nor the number of basepoints, and
  leaves `HF̂_st(D)` unchanged (`TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.hatStableClass_stabilize`).
* **Type `b`.** Adding a basepoint in a region already containing one
  (`TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.addBasepoint`) replaces the hat complex by its tensor product
  with `W`, so it replaces `\widetilde{HF}(D)` by `\widetilde{HF}(D) ⊗ W`
  (`TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.hatHomologyAddBasepointEquiv`) and adds one basepoint, which
  leaves `HF̂_st(D)` unchanged (`TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.hatStableClass_addBasepoint`).

For the genus-one diagram of `L(p, q)` the class is `[𝔽^p, 1]`, recorded as `p / 2`
(`TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.hatStableClass_lensSpace`), and for `S¹ × S²` with the basepoint in
the annulus it is `[𝔽², 1]`, recorded as `1`
(`TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.hatStableClass_circleTimesSphere`). The diagram of `S³` is the lens
space diagram with `p = 1`, of class `[𝔽, 1]`, which differs from that of `S¹ × S²`.

## Main definitions

* `TauCeti.stableClass`: the stable class of a pair `(V, b)`, recorded as `dim V / 2 ^ b`.
* `TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.hatHomology`: the hat homology `\widetilde{HF}(D)` of a diagram
  whose hat differential squares to zero.
* `TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.hatStableClass`: the stable hat invariant `HF̂_st(D)`.

## Main results

* `TauCeti.finrank_tensorProduct_piTensorProduct_prod`: `V ⊗ W^{⊗ k}` has dimension
  `dim V * 2 ^ k`.
* `TauCeti.stableClass_tensorProduct_prod`: the generating move `(V ⊗ W, b + 1) ~ (V, b)`.
* `TauCeti.stableClass_tensorProduct_piTensorProduct`: its `k`-fold iterate
  `(V ⊗ W^{⊗ k}, b + k) ~ (V, b)`.
* `TauCeti.stableClass_eq_stableClass_add_iff`: equal classes are related by one move.
* `TauCeti.stableClass_eq_stableClass_iff`: two pairs have the same class exactly when
  `dim V * 2 ^ b' = dim V' * 2 ^ b`.
* `TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.hatStableClass_stabilize` and
  `TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.hatStableClass_addBasepoint`: the stable class is invariant under
  stabilizations of types `g` and `b`.

## References

* P. Ozsváth, A. Stipsicz and Z. Szabó, *Combinatorial Heegaard Floer homology and nice Heegaard
  diagrams*, Adv. Math. **231** (2012), [arXiv:0912.0830](https://arxiv.org/abs/0912.0830),
  Definitions 1.1 and 6.13 (the stable class) and Theorem 7.1 (its invariance under nice moves).
-/

public section

open Module
open scoped TensorProduct

namespace TauCeti

/-! ### Stable classes of pairs -/

section StableClass

variable (K : Type*) [Semiring K] (V : Type*) [AddCommMonoid V] [Module K V]
  {V' : Type*} [AddCommMonoid V'] [Module K V']

/-- The **stable class** `[V, b]` of a vector space `V` and a natural number `b`, under the
equivalence relation generated by `(V ⊗ (K × K)^{⊗ k}, b + k) ~ (V, b)`, recorded as the rational
number `dim V / 2 ^ b`. For finite-dimensional vector spaces over a field this number is a complete
invariant of the class (`TauCeti.stableClass_eq_stableClass_add_iff`). In general it is only an
invariant: for instance every infinite-dimensional `V` has `finrank K V = 0`, so value `0`. -/
noncomputable def stableClass (b : ℕ) : ℚ :=
  finrank K V / 2 ^ b

theorem stableClass_def (b : ℕ) : stableClass K V b = finrank K V / 2 ^ b :=
  (rfl)

variable {K V}

/-- Isomorphic spaces have the same stable class. -/
theorem _root_.LinearEquiv.stableClass_eq (e : V ≃ₗ[K] V') (b : ℕ) :
    stableClass K V b = stableClass K V' b := by
  rw [stableClass_def, stableClass_def, e.finrank_eq]

/-- Two pairs have the same stable class exactly when `dim V * 2 ^ b' = dim V' * 2 ^ b`. -/
theorem stableClass_eq_stableClass_iff {b b' : ℕ} :
    stableClass K V b = stableClass K V' b' ↔ finrank K V * 2 ^ b' = finrank K V' * 2 ^ b := by
  rw [stableClass_def, stableClass_def, div_eq_div_iff (by positivity) (by positivity)]
  exact_mod_cast Iff.rfl

end StableClass

section Field

variable (K : Type*) [Field K] (V : Type*) [AddCommGroup V] [Module K V]
  {V' : Type*} [AddCommGroup V'] [Module K V']

/-- The dimension of `V ⊗ W^{⊗ k}` with `W = K × K` is `dim V * 2 ^ k`. -/
theorem finrank_tensorProduct_piTensorProduct_prod (k : ℕ) :
    finrank K (V ⊗[K] (⨂[K] _ : Fin k, K × K)) = finrank K V * 2 ^ k := by
  simp [finrank_tensorProduct, finrank_piTensorProduct]

/-- The **generating move** `(V ⊗ W, b + 1) ~ (V, b)` with `W = K × K`. -/
@[simp]
theorem stableClass_tensorProduct_prod (b : ℕ) :
    stableClass K (V ⊗[K] (K × K)) (b + 1) = stableClass K V b := by
  rw [stableClass_eq_stableClass_iff, finrank_tensorProduct, finrank_prod, finrank_self, pow_succ]
  ring

/-- The `k`-fold **generating move** `(V ⊗ W^{⊗ k}, b + k) ~ (V, b)` with `W = K × K`. -/
@[simp]
theorem stableClass_tensorProduct_piTensorProduct (b k : ℕ) :
    stableClass K (V ⊗[K] (⨂[K] _ : Fin k, K × K)) (b + k) = stableClass K V b := by
  rw [stableClass_eq_stableClass_iff, finrank_tensorProduct_piTensorProduct_prod, pow_add]
  ring

variable {K V}

/-- **The stable class is complete.** Two finite-dimensional pairs with `b ≤ b + k` have the same
stable class exactly when they are related by one generating move, `V' ≅ V ⊗ W^{⊗ k}`. So the
equivalence relation generated by the moves relates two pairs exactly when their stable classes
agree. -/
theorem stableClass_eq_stableClass_add_iff [FiniteDimensional K V] [FiniteDimensional K V']
    {b k : ℕ} :
    stableClass K V b = stableClass K V' (b + k) ↔
      Nonempty (V' ≃ₗ[K] V ⊗[K] (⨂[K] _ : Fin k, K × K)) := by
  constructor
  · intro h
    refine ⟨LinearEquiv.ofFinrankEq _ _ ?_⟩
    rw [stableClass_eq_stableClass_iff, pow_add] at h
    rw [finrank_tensorProduct_piTensorProduct_prod]
    exact (Nat.eq_of_mul_eq_mul_right (pow_pos two_pos b) (by linarith)).symm
  · rintro ⟨e⟩
    rw [e.stableClass_eq, stableClass_tensorProduct_piTensorProduct]

end Field

/-! ### The stable hat invariant of a diagram -/

namespace HeegaardRegionSystem

universe u v w

variable {n : ℕ} {Point : Type u} {Region : Type v} {Basepoint : Type w}
  {H : HeegaardRegionSystem n Point Region Basepoint}

section Homology

variable [Fintype Point] [DecidableEq Region] [Fintype Region]

variable (H) in
/-- The **hat homology** `\widetilde{HF}(D) = ker ∂ ⧸ im ∂` of a diagram whose hat differential
`∂`, for the region Euler characteristics `χ`, squares to zero. -/
abbrev hatHomology (χ : Region → ℤ) (hd : H.hatDifferential χ ∘ₗ H.hatDifferential χ = 0) :
    Type _ :=
  (H.hatDifferential χ).homology hd

variable (H) in
/-- The **stable hat invariant** `[\widetilde{HF}(D), b(D)]` of a diagram whose hat differential
squares to zero: the stable class of its hat homology with the number of its basepoints, recorded
as `dim \widetilde{HF}(D) / 2 ^ b(D)` (`TauCeti.stableClass`). No niceness is assumed: for a nice
diagram (`TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.IsNice`) this is the Ozsváth–Stipsicz–Szabó invariant
`HF̂_st(D)`, and for other diagrams it is just the stable class of the homology of the count of
index-one domains. -/
noncomputable def hatStableClass [Fintype Basepoint] (χ : Region → ℤ)
    (hd : H.hatDifferential χ ∘ₗ H.hatDifferential χ = 0) : ℚ :=
  stableClass (ZMod 2) (H.hatHomology χ hd) (Fintype.card Basepoint)

theorem hatStableClass_def [Fintype Basepoint] (χ : Region → ℤ)
    (hd : H.hatDifferential χ ∘ₗ H.hatDifferential χ = 0) :
    H.hatStableClass χ hd = stableClass (ZMod 2) (H.hatHomology χ hd) (Fintype.card Basepoint) :=
  (rfl)

/-- When the hat differential vanishes, the hat homology is the whole hat chain group, and the
stable hat invariant is the number of generators divided by `2 ^ b(D)`. -/
theorem hatStableClass_of_hatDifferential_eq_zero [Fintype Basepoint] {χ : Region → ℤ}
    (h : H.hatDifferential χ = 0) (hd : H.hatDifferential χ ∘ₗ H.hatDifferential χ = 0) :
    H.hatStableClass χ hd = Fintype.card H.Generator / 2 ^ Fintype.card Basepoint := by
  rw [hatStableClass_def, ((H.hatDifferential χ).homologyEquivOfEqZero hd h).stableClass_eq,
    stableClass_def, finrank_finsupp_self]

end Homology

section Stabilize

variable [Fintype Point] [DecidableEq Region] [Fintype Region] (r₀ : Region) {χ : Region → ℤ}

/-- The hat differential of a stabilized diagram squares to zero when that of the original one
does. -/
theorem hatDifferential_stabilize_comp_self_eq_zero
    (hd : H.hatDifferential χ ∘ₗ H.hatDifferential χ = 0) :
    (H.stabilize r₀).hatDifferential (stabilizeEuler χ r₀) ∘ₗ
      (H.stabilize r₀).hatDifferential (stabilizeEuler χ r₀) = 0 := by
  rw [((H.stabilizeChainEquiv r₀).eq_conjRingEquiv_apply_iff (H.hatDifferential χ)).mpr
    (H.hatDifferential_comp_stabilizeChainEquiv r₀)]
  exact (H.stabilizeChainEquiv r₀).conjRingEquiv_apply_comp_self hd

/-- **Stabilization does not change the hat homology**: the identification of hat chain groups
`TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.stabilizeChainEquiv` induces
`\widetilde{HF}(D) ≅ \widetilde{HF}(D')` for the stabilized diagram `D'`. -/
noncomputable def hatHomologyStabilizeEquiv
    (hd : H.hatDifferential χ ∘ₗ H.hatDifferential χ = 0) :
    H.hatHomology χ hd ≃ₗ[ZMod 2]
      (H.stabilize r₀).hatHomology (stabilizeEuler χ r₀)
        (H.hatDifferential_stabilize_comp_self_eq_zero r₀ hd) :=
  (H.stabilizeChainEquiv r₀).homologyEquiv hd _ (H.hatDifferential_comp_stabilizeChainEquiv r₀).symm

/-- `TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.hatHomologyStabilizeEquiv` sends the class of a cycle `z` to the
class of its image `TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.stabilizeChainEquiv r₀ z`. -/
@[simp]
theorem hatHomologyStabilizeEquiv_mk (hd : H.hatDifferential χ ∘ₗ H.hatDifferential χ = 0)
    (z : LinearMap.ker (H.hatDifferential χ)) :
    H.hatHomologyStabilizeEquiv r₀ hd (Submodule.Quotient.mk z) =
      Submodule.Quotient.mk ⟨H.stabilizeChainEquiv r₀ z,
        LinearMap.map_mem_ker_of_comp_eq (H.stabilizeChainEquiv r₀).toLinearMap
          (H.hatDifferential_comp_stabilizeChainEquiv r₀).symm z.property⟩ :=
  LinearEquiv.homologyEquiv_mk _ _ _ _ z

/-- **The stable hat invariant is unchanged by a stabilization of type `g`.** -/
@[simp]
theorem hatStableClass_stabilize [Fintype Basepoint]
    (hd : H.hatDifferential χ ∘ₗ H.hatDifferential χ = 0) :
    (H.stabilize r₀).hatStableClass (stabilizeEuler χ r₀)
        (H.hatDifferential_stabilize_comp_self_eq_zero r₀ hd) =
      H.hatStableClass χ hd :=
  ((H.hatHomologyStabilizeEquiv r₀ hd).stableClass_eq _).symm

end Stabilize

section AddBasepoint

variable {r₀ : Region} {χ : Region → ℤ}

variable (H) in
/-- The identification of the hat chain group of the diagram with an added basepoint with
`CF̂(D) ⊗ (𝔽₂ × 𝔽₂)`: the inverse of `TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.addBasepointChainEquiv`
followed by the identification `(Fin 2 →₀ 𝔽₂) ≅ 𝔽₂ × 𝔽₂` of the second factor. -/
noncomputable def addBasepointProdEquiv (r₀ : Region) :
    ((H.addBasepoint r₀).Generator →₀ ZMod 2) ≃ₗ[ZMod 2]
      (H.Generator →₀ ZMod 2) ⊗[ZMod 2] (ZMod 2 × ZMod 2) :=
  (H.addBasepointChainEquiv r₀).symm.trans
    (((Finsupp.linearEquivFunOnFinite (ZMod 2) (ZMod 2) (Fin 2)).trans
      (LinearEquiv.finTwoArrow (ZMod 2) (ZMod 2))).lTensor _)

/-- The inverse of `TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.addBasepointProdEquiv` sends `c ⊗ (a, b)` to the
image of `c ⊗ (a • [0] + b • [1])` under `TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.addBasepointChainEquiv`. -/
@[simp]
theorem addBasepointProdEquiv_symm_tmul (c : H.Generator →₀ ZMod 2) (w : ZMod 2 × ZMod 2) :
    (H.addBasepointProdEquiv r₀).symm (c ⊗ₜ w) =
      H.addBasepointChainEquiv r₀ (c ⊗ₜ (Finsupp.single 0 w.1 + Finsupp.single 1 w.2)) := by
  rw [LinearEquiv.symm_apply_eq, addBasepointProdEquiv, LinearEquiv.trans_apply,
    LinearEquiv.symm_apply_apply, LinearEquiv.lTensor_tmul]
  congr 1
  ext <;> simp

variable [Fintype Point] [DecidableEq Region] [Fintype Region]

/-- Under `TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.addBasepointProdEquiv`, the hat differential of the
diagram with a basepoint added in a region containing a basepoint is `∂ ⊗ 1`. -/
theorem addBasepointProdEquiv_comp_hatDifferential (hr₀ : r₀ ∈ Set.range H.basepoint) :
    (H.addBasepointProdEquiv r₀).toLinearMap ∘ₗ
        (H.addBasepoint r₀).hatDifferential (addBasepointEuler χ r₀) =
      (H.hatDifferential χ).rTensor (ZMod 2 × ZMod 2) ∘ₗ
        (H.addBasepointProdEquiv r₀).toLinearMap := by
  refine LinearMap.ext fun x => ?_
  obtain ⟨t, rfl⟩ := (H.addBasepointChainEquiv r₀).surjective x
  have h := congr($(H.hatDifferential_comp_addBasepointChainEquiv (χ := χ) r₀ hr₀) t)
  simp only [LinearMap.comp_apply, LinearEquiv.coe_coe] at h
  simp only [LinearMap.comp_apply, LinearEquiv.coe_coe, h, addBasepointProdEquiv,
    LinearEquiv.trans_apply, LinearEquiv.symm_apply_apply]
  clear h
  induction t using TensorProduct.inductionOn with
  | tmul c w => simp
  | add a b ha hb => simp only [map_add, ha, hb]

/-- The inverse of `TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.addBasepointProdEquiv` carries `∂ ⊗ 1` to the
hat differential of the diagram with a basepoint added in a region containing a basepoint. -/
theorem hatDifferential_comp_addBasepointProdEquiv_symm (hr₀ : r₀ ∈ Set.range H.basepoint) :
    (H.addBasepoint r₀).hatDifferential (addBasepointEuler χ r₀) ∘ₗ
        (H.addBasepointProdEquiv r₀).symm.toLinearMap =
      (H.addBasepointProdEquiv r₀).symm.toLinearMap ∘ₗ
        (H.hatDifferential χ).rTensor (ZMod 2 × ZMod 2) := by
  rw [LinearEquiv.eq_toLinearMap_symm_comp, ← LinearMap.comp_assoc,
    addBasepointProdEquiv_comp_hatDifferential hr₀]
  exact (LinearEquiv.comp_toLinearMap_symm_eq _ _).mpr rfl

/-- The hat differential of the diagram with a basepoint added in a region containing a basepoint
squares to zero when that of the original diagram does. -/
theorem hatDifferential_addBasepoint_comp_self_eq_zero (hr₀ : r₀ ∈ Set.range H.basepoint)
    (hd : H.hatDifferential χ ∘ₗ H.hatDifferential χ = 0) :
    (H.addBasepoint r₀).hatDifferential (addBasepointEuler χ r₀) ∘ₗ
      (H.addBasepoint r₀).hatDifferential (addBasepointEuler χ r₀) = 0 := by
  rw [((H.addBasepointChainEquiv r₀).eq_conjRingEquiv_apply_iff _).mpr
    (H.hatDifferential_comp_addBasepointChainEquiv r₀ hr₀)]
  exact (H.addBasepointChainEquiv r₀).conjRingEquiv_apply_comp_self
    ((H.hatDifferential χ).rTensor_comp_rTensor_eq_zero _ hd)

/-- **Adding a basepoint tensors the hat homology with `W`.** For a basepoint added in a region
containing a basepoint, a stabilization of type `b`, the hat homology of the new diagram is
`\widetilde{HF}(D) ⊗ W` with `W = 𝔽₂ × 𝔽₂`. -/
noncomputable def hatHomologyAddBasepointEquiv (hr₀ : r₀ ∈ Set.range H.basepoint)
    (hd : H.hatDifferential χ ∘ₗ H.hatDifferential χ = 0) :
    (H.addBasepoint r₀).hatHomology (addBasepointEuler χ r₀)
        (H.hatDifferential_addBasepoint_comp_self_eq_zero hr₀ hd) ≃ₗ[ZMod 2]
      H.hatHomology χ hd ⊗[ZMod 2] (ZMod 2 × ZMod 2) :=
  ((H.addBasepointProdEquiv r₀).homologyEquiv _ _
      (addBasepointProdEquiv_comp_hatDifferential hr₀)).trans
    ((H.hatDifferential χ).homologyRTensorProdEquiv hd)

/-- The inverse of `TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.hatHomologyAddBasepointEquiv` sends the class of
a cycle `z` tensored with `w` to the class of the cycle
`(TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.addBasepointProdEquiv r₀).symm (z ⊗ w)`. -/
@[simp]
theorem hatHomologyAddBasepointEquiv_symm_mk_tmul (hr₀ : r₀ ∈ Set.range H.basepoint)
    (hd : H.hatDifferential χ ∘ₗ H.hatDifferential χ = 0) (z : LinearMap.ker (H.hatDifferential χ))
    (w : ZMod 2 × ZMod 2) :
    (H.hatHomologyAddBasepointEquiv hr₀ hd).symm (Submodule.Quotient.mk z ⊗ₜ w) =
      Submodule.Quotient.mk ⟨(H.addBasepointProdEquiv r₀).symm ((z : H.Generator →₀ ZMod 2) ⊗ₜ w),
        LinearMap.map_mem_ker_of_comp_eq (H.addBasepointProdEquiv r₀).symm.toLinearMap
          (H.hatDifferential_comp_addBasepointProdEquiv_symm hr₀).symm
          (LinearMap.tmul_mem_ker_rTensor z.property w)⟩ := by
  simp [hatHomologyAddBasepointEquiv, LinearEquiv.symm_apply_eq, -addBasepointProdEquiv_symm_tmul]

/-- The hat homology doubles in dimension when a basepoint is added in a region containing a
basepoint. -/
theorem finrank_hatHomology_addBasepoint (hr₀ : r₀ ∈ Set.range H.basepoint)
    (hd : H.hatDifferential χ ∘ₗ H.hatDifferential χ = 0) :
    finrank (ZMod 2) ((H.addBasepoint r₀).hatHomology (addBasepointEuler χ r₀)
        (H.hatDifferential_addBasepoint_comp_self_eq_zero hr₀ hd)) =
      2 * finrank (ZMod 2) (H.hatHomology χ hd) := by
  rw [(H.hatHomologyAddBasepointEquiv hr₀ hd).finrank_eq, finrank_tensorProduct, finrank_prod,
    finrank_self, mul_comm]

/-- **The stable hat invariant is unchanged by a stabilization of type `b`**: adding a basepoint in
a region containing a basepoint tensors `\widetilde{HF}(D)` with `W` and adds one basepoint. -/
@[simp]
theorem hatStableClass_addBasepoint [Fintype Basepoint] (hr₀ : r₀ ∈ Set.range H.basepoint)
    (hd : H.hatDifferential χ ∘ₗ H.hatDifferential χ = 0) :
    (H.addBasepoint r₀).hatStableClass (addBasepointEuler χ r₀)
        (H.hatDifferential_addBasepoint_comp_self_eq_zero hr₀ hd) =
      H.hatStableClass χ hd := by
  rw [hatStableClass_def, hatStableClass_def, Fintype.card_sum, Fintype.card_unit,
    (H.hatHomologyAddBasepointEquiv hr₀ hd).stableClass_eq, stableClass_tensorProduct_prod]

end AddBasepoint

/-! ### Examples -/

section Examples

/-- The hat differential of the genus-one diagram of `L(p, q)` squares to zero, since it
vanishes. -/
theorem hatDifferential_lensSpace_comp_self_eq_zero (p : ℕ) [NeZero p] (q : (ZMod p)ˣ)
    (r : ZMod p) :
    (lensSpace p q r).hatDifferential 1 ∘ₗ (lensSpace p q r).hatDifferential 1 = 0 := by
  simp

/-- The stable hat invariant of the genus-one diagram of `L(p, q)` is `[𝔽^p, 1]`, recorded as
`p / 2`: one generator for each `Spin^c` structure and one basepoint. -/
theorem hatStableClass_lensSpace (p : ℕ) [NeZero p] (q : (ZMod p)ˣ) (r : ZMod p) :
    (lensSpace p q r).hatStableClass 1 (hatDifferential_lensSpace_comp_self_eq_zero p q r) =
      p / 2 := by
  rw [hatStableClass_of_hatDifferential_eq_zero
      (hatDifferential_lensSpace (p := p) (q := q) (r := r)),
    ← Fintype.card_of_bijective (lensSpaceGenerator_bijective (p := p) (q := q) (r := r)),
    ZMod.card]
  simp

/-- The hat differential of the genus-one diagram of `S¹ × S²` with the basepoint in the annulus
squares to zero, since it vanishes. -/
theorem hatDifferential_circleTimesSphere_comp_self_eq_zero :
    (circleTimesSphere 0).hatDifferential ![0, 1, 1] ∘ₗ
      (circleTimesSphere 0).hatDifferential ![0, 1, 1] = 0 := by
  simp [hatDifferential_circleTimesSphere_zero]

/-- The stable hat invariant of the genus-one diagram of `S¹ × S²` with the basepoint in the
annulus is `[𝔽², 1]`, recorded as `1`. It differs from the invariant `[𝔽, 1]` of the diagram of
`S³`, the lens space diagram with `p = 1`, of value `1 / 2`
(`TauCeti.HeegaardRegionSystem.hatStableClass_lensSpace`). -/
theorem hatStableClass_circleTimesSphere :
    (circleTimesSphere 0).hatStableClass ![0, 1, 1]
        hatDifferential_circleTimesSphere_comp_self_eq_zero = 1 := by
  rw [hatStableClass_of_hatDifferential_eq_zero hatDifferential_circleTimesSphere_zero,
    ← Fintype.card_of_bijective (circleTimesSphereGenerator_bijective 0)]
  norm_num

